  "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nAdds a glossary that clarifies how A.T.O.M uses Cell, sector, site, tower record, candidate, and dataset identity. Links it from setup, inventory, first-use help, FAQ, and documentation navigation.\r\n\r\n## Linked issue\r\n\r\nCloses Berk-Unsal/atom#80\r\n\r\n## Affected surfaces\r\n\r\n- `docs/terminology.md` and generated `docs/terminology.html`\r\n- Getting Started, Features, FAQ, and documentation overview\r\n- Shared documentation navigation and search index\r\n- `CHANGELOG.md` and documentation source catalog\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\n- [x] Relevant checks run: `docs/build-reference-pages.sh` completed; `docs/validate_docs.py` passed (58 HTML pages and 42 API paths); `docs/validate_claims.py` passed; `docs/classify_docs.py` passed; `git diff --check` passed.\r\n- [x] Checks skipped: frontend/backend test suites; no application code changed.\r\n\r\n## Screenshots (UI changes only)\r\n\r\nN/A \u2014 documentation-only change.\r\n\r\n## Boundary notes (RF / scope / persistence / compatibility changes)\r\n\r\nNo RF, API, schema, or persistence behavior changed. Existing API names such as `towers[]` remain compatible. The glossary states that dataset records and candidates do not verify physical sites or feasibility.\r\n\r\n## Changelog\r\n\r\nAdded an Unreleased documentation entry in `CHANGELOG.md`.",
